dsh-digital-earth
================

This product bundles CesiumJS 1.147.0 (vendor/cesium), which is distributed
under the Apache License, Version 2.0. A copy of that license is included at
vendor/cesium/LICENSE.md; Cesium's own third-party notices are under
vendor/cesium/ThirdParty.

Cesium® is a registered trademark of Cesium GS, Inc. This plugin is not
affiliated with or endorsed by Cesium GS, Inc.

Imagery and elevation are streamed at runtime from public ArcGIS services and
remain subject to Esri's terms of use.

The loading globe's bundled land mask is derived from the Natural Earth II
textures included with CesiumJS (vendor/cesium/Assets/Textures/NaturalEarthII).
Natural Earth raster data is in the public domain: https://www.naturalearthdata.com/

Place search is streamed at runtime from the provider the user selects:
Tianditu (https://cloudcenter.tianditu.gov.cn/) and Amap
(https://console.amap.com/dev/key/app) with a user-supplied key, Photon
(https://photon.komoot.io/), or an OpenStreetMap Nominatim instance
(https://operations.osmfoundation.org/policies/nominatim/). Tianditu and Amap
data remain subject to their own service terms. Photon and Nominatim results
contain data © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open Database
License (ODbL): https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

Users may add their own provider instance (an own server, a mirror or a proxy) by
supplying its service URL in Settings; requests then go to that URL and the terms
of that service apply.

Service availability, data content and terms of use are the responsibility of
each provider, not of this plugin or its developers; confirm and comply with the
applicable provider terms before use.

The plugin itself sends no telemetry and collects no usage statistics. Only the
features the user starts send data out: AI 2D instance extraction and "send view
to AI" upload a nadir panel capture to the chosen vision-model service (the DSH
model or a custom OpenAI-compatible endpoint), and place search sends the typed
query to the selected provider.
